{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,15.359,1.643,1.471,"India Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"15 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,20.598,3.651,3.268,"Indian Hotels"],[13.889,14.731,32.799,2.373,2.124,"Record quarter, soft base, full price"],[13.889,20.845,52.934,1.809,1.634,"Indian Hotels (IHCL) has risen 18% since its Q2 FY27 results on 21 October"],[13.889,22.289,52.936,1.809,1.634,"(NIFTY: 10%) and sits near a record. Revenue grew 22% to ₹2,484 cr, net profit"],[13.889,23.733,52.987,1.809,1.634,"23% to ₹349 cr, and FY27 revenue-growth guidance went up to 15-17% from"],[13.889,25.177,52.951,1.809,1.634,"12-14%. The quarter was strong; the comparison flatters it. A year ago rain,"],[13.889,26.621,52.934,1.809,1.634,"fewer wedding dates and rooms shut for renovation held growth back. This year"],[13.889,28.065,52.966,1.809,1.634,"Delhi hosted the BRICS summit and Taj Palace had its renovated rooms back:"],[13.889,29.509,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Delhi revenue rose 51%, Mumbai 12%. Domestic RevPAR rose 25%. Over two"],[13.889,30.954,43.056,1.809,1.634,"years revenue has grown 17% a year. Air-catering profit fell 37%."],[13.889,33.439,52.931,1.809,1.634,"1) In H2 FY27E hotel revenue grows 16% (guidance implies 14-18%) and"],[13.889,34.883,52.957,1.809,1.634,"catering is flat as airlines cut schedules. Our FY27E EPS of ₹15.27 is 6% below"],[13.889,36.328,52.959,1.809,1.634,"consensus, which needs H2 profit up 26% on revenue up 15%. 2) In FY28E"],[13.889,37.772,52.966,1.809,1.634,"hotels grow 12%: more wedding dates, against the BRICS quarter. Oriental"],[13.889,39.216,52.964,1.809,1.634,"Hotels merges in from 1 April 2027 (2.32 cr new shares), adding ₹560 cr of"],[13.889,40.684,52.992,1.809,1.634,"revenue. 3) Management fees pass ₹1,000 cr in FY28E; 94% of the 34,800-key"],[13.889,42.128,46.763,1.809,1.634,"pipeline is capital-light. EPS grows 18%, 17% and 14% in FY27E-29E."],[13.889,44.59,52.934,1.809,1.634,"Our Dec-27 target of ₹690 averages two methods. IHCL’s own three-year"],[13.889,46.034,52.934,1.809,1.634,"average P/E of 51x, on earnings twelve months ahead, gives ₹1,012. A ten-year"],[13.889,47.502,52.951,1.809,1.634,"DCF of hotel and catering cash flows at a 12% cost of equity, plus net cash,"],[13.889,48.946,52.931,1.809,1.634,"gives ₹367. The gap is the argument: at ₹890 the shares need free cash flow to"],[13.889,50.39,52.931,1.809,1.634,"grow 28% a year to FY37E; we forecast 11%. Listed hotel peers trade at 23.5x"],[13.889,51.834,52.931,1.809,1.634,"forward earnings, IHCL at 46x. The consensus target of ₹876 is also below the"],[13.889,53.278,52.992,1.809,1.634,"price, though 25 of 28 brokers say buy. What would prove us wrong: occupancy"],[13.889,54.722,52.987,1.809,1.634,"holding above 80%; fees growing faster than 20% a year. Downside: room"],[13.889,56.167,31.23,1.809,1.634,"supply in smaller cities, set to grow 12% a year."],[13.889,58.654,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[15.268,67.265,1.489,1.022,0.915,"500"],[15.268,65.498,1.489,1.022,0.915,"600"],[15.268,63.73,1.489,1.022,0.915,"700"],[15.268,61.962,1.489,1.022,0.915,"800"],[15.268,60.195,1.489,1.022,0.915,"900"],[18.306,67.96,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[22.929,67.96,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.701,67.96,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[32.473,67.96,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[18.975,69.131,2.57,1.275,1.111,"IHCL ("],[21.548,69.157,0.618,1.241,1.111,"₹"],[22.161,69.131,0.303,1.275,1.111,")"],[25.245,69.131,7.901,1.275,1.111,"NIFTY 50 (rebased)"],[20.291,70.291,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[25.561,70.291,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[30.279,70.291,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,70.291,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,71.356,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[19.372,71.356,2.811,1.387,1.209,"21.0%"],[24.09,71.356,2.811,1.387,1.209,"22.9%"],[28.808,71.356,2.811,1.387,1.209,"23.4%"],[33.527,71.356,2.811,1.387,1.209,"24.6%"],[15.492,72.421,1.476,1.3